          "value": "Prokaryotic & Eukaryotic",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Cell Control Center",
          "value": "Nucleus",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Powerhouse Unit",
          "value": "Mitochondria",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "tjggql8"
    },
    {
      "id": "mc2sucx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Discovery of the Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Cells are the structural, functional, and biological units of all living organisms.",
        "Cell Theory postulates that all living beings are composed of cells and new cells originate from pre-existing cells.",
        "Prokaryotic cells lack a defined membrane-bound nucleus, whereas eukaryotic cells contain a well-defined nucleus and membrane-bound organelles.",
        "The cell membrane functions as a selectively permeable barrier regulating entry and exit of substances.",
        "Plant cells contain cell walls, plastids/chloroplasts, and large central vacuoles, which are absent or modified in animal cells."
      ],
      "id": "78rjjh2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gisjvsu",
      "content": "• Robert Hooke discovered the cell in 1665 while observing cork under a microscope."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yf6rdp6",
      "content": "• He described the small compartments as 'cells'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xpgbd9c",
      "content": "• Anton van Leeuwenhoek later observed living cells using a microscope."
    },
    {
      "id": "78oah84",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Cell Theory"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a47o3ny",
      "content": "• All living organisms are composed of cells."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h3du4uw",
      "content": "• The cell is the basic unit of life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "khm5qb9",
      "content": "• All cells arise from pre-existing cells."
    },
    {
      "id": "5pp7101",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Types of Cells"
    },
    {
